{
 "header": {
  "width": 400,
  "height": 400,
  "apiLevel": 7,
  "contentDescription": "Three watch wheels of eighteen, eleven and twenty-four teeth, turning in mesh. Each wheel's rim is a single polar expression in its tooth count, and the wheels stay engaged because their phases are locked by the gear ratio rather than animated separately."
 },
 "root": [
  {
   "box": {
    "modifiers": [
     "fillMaxSize"
    ],
    "children": [
     {
      "type": "canvas",
      "modifiers": [
       "fillMaxSize"
      ],
      "commands": [
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "GEAR RECIPE - how these wheels are made and why they mesh."
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": ""
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "A wheel of N teeth is one polar curve. With theta the angle round the wheel and"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "phi the wheel's rotation:"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "  u     = fract(N * (theta - phi) / 2pi)        position within one tooth pitch, 0..1"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "  s     = clamp((hr - abs(u - 0.5)) / (hr - ht))    trapezoid, tooth centred at u=0.5"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "  tooth = 0.5 - 0.5 * cos(pi * s)               eased: curved flanks, rounded tip"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "  r     = rp - ded*m + (add + ded)*m * tooth"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "then x = cx + r*cos(theta), y = cy + r*sin(theta) over theta = 0..2pi."
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": ""
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "m is the module: pitch diameter per tooth. rp = m*N/2 is the pitch radius."
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "add (addendum) is how far a tooth rises above the pitch circle, ded (dedendum) how"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "far the root falls below it. ht and hr are the tooth's half-thickness at tip and at"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "root as a fraction of the pitch; hr > ht splays the flanks outward going down, as a"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "real tooth does."
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": ""
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "This document uses m=5.20 px, add=0.95, ded=1.20, ht=0.13, hr=0.29. Those were"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "chosen by measuring interference, not by eye: sample both outlines densely, test"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "each point of one against the other's polar radius, and sweep a full tooth pitch of"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "rotation. Worst clearance here is about +0.09 of a module, a real backlash figure."
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "Fatter teeth jam. Below about nine teeth this profile interferes with itself, which"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "is the same undercutting limit that stops real gears having tiny tooth counts."
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": ""
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "TWO WHEELS MESH when they share a module. That fixes the centre distance:"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "  C = m * (NA + NB) / 2"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "and the ratio: B turns NA/NB times as fast as A, in the opposite direction."
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": ""
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "THE PHASE is the part that is easy to get wrong. With B's centre at angle beta as"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "seen from A:"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "  phi_B = beta + pi - pi/NB + (NA/NB) * (beta - phi_A)"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "The invariant this maintains at the contact point is a REFLECTION, u_B = 0.5 - u_A,"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "not a translation: at A's contact point increasing theta runs one way round the rim"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "and at B's it runs the other, so the tooth pattern is mirrored. Deriving it as a"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "translation gives phi_B running forwards with phi_A and the wheels jam solid except"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "at the instants when teeth happen to line up - which a clearance test only catches"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "if it samples BETWEEN those instants, not just at them."
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": ""
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "For a train, each wheel's phase stays linear in the first wheel's, so phi_i can be"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "folded to a single constant plus a multiple of phi_0 - as the p0/p1/p2 variables"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "below are."
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": ""
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "ONE SYNTAX TRAP: the tooth term must be parenthesised where it is multiplied in."
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "Written as rroot + height * 0.5 - 0.5*cos(...) it parses as (rroot + height*0.5)"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "minus a half-amplitude cosine, which draws a near-perfect circle with a half-pixel"
        }
       },
       {
        "rem": {
         "text": "wobble - and renders without complaint, so nothing tells you the gear is gone."
        }
       },
       {
        "paint": {
         "ops": [
          {
           "color": "#FF13161C"
          },
          {
           "style": "fill"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
